"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. Favorable findings include negative surgical margins and non-invasion of the seminal vesicles. The surgical pathology reported a Gleason 3+5 (ISUP grade group 4) and pT3a stage with extraprostatic extension. Countervailing factors include the absence of lymph node removal, resulting in an uncharacterized nodal status, as no nodes were sampled. The biopsy showed an Acinar growth pattern, which is noted, though the biopsy grade was the same as the prostatectomy specimen. The preoperative PSA was 6.4. The lack of documented postoperative PSA or follow-up significantly widens the uncertainty regarding the trajectory of recurrence. Missing nodal sampling further complicates the assessment of local control. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and their subsequent trend is crucial for refining this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 56.82 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 36.93–76.70 months; its coverage has not been validated."
